<!-- PAGE HERO -->
<div class="ph">
  <div class="ph-in">
    <div class="eyebrow">Service</div>
    <h1>Ductwork &amp; Airflow Service in Murrieta, Temecula &amp; SW Riverside County</h1>
    <p>Duct design, installation, repair, and sealing — plus airflow diagnosis to fix hot-and-cold rooms, weak vents, and energy lost to leaky ducts.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- MAIN SERVICE CONTENT -->
<section class="sv-page">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sd-standalone fi">
      <div class="sd-hd">
        <div class="sd-ic">🛠️</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Ductwork &amp; Airflow</h2>
          <p>Design, installation, repair &amp; sealing to fix airflow problems</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="sd-bd">Your ductwork is the part of the HVAC system nobody sees and almost nobody thinks about — until one room is always hot, another is always cold, the vents barely push air, or the energy bill keeps climbing while the equipment seems fine. That's because a heating and cooling system is only as good as the ducts delivering the air. Poorly designed, undersized, disconnected, crushed, or leaky ducts force your equipment to work harder and still leave you uncomfortable. A surprising amount of conditioned air in a typical home never reaches the rooms — it leaks out into attics and crawlspaces along the way.</p>

      <p class="sd-bd">We handle the whole ducted side of the system. That means designing and installing new ductwork for additions, remodels, and new construction; repairing and replacing damaged or aging duct runs; sealing leaks so the air you paid to condition actually reaches your rooms; and diagnosing airflow problems when the equipment checks out but the comfort doesn't. When a customer calls about a room that won't cool, the answer often isn't a new AC — it's a duct problem, and replacing the equipment wouldn't have fixed it. We find the actual cause first, then tell you what it'll take to fix it.</p>

      <div class="sd-feats">
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Ductwork design &amp; new installation</div></div>
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Duct repair &amp; replacement</div></div>
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Duct sealing &amp; leak repair</div></div>
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Airflow diagnosis &amp; balancing</div></div>
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Hot &amp; cold room corrections</div></div>
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Return air &amp; vent improvements</div></div>
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Duct inspection &amp; assessment</div></div>
        <div class="sd-f"><div class="sd-f-ck"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="5 12 10 17 19 8"/></svg></div><div class="sd-f-tx">Honest diagnosis before you replace equipment</div></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Local relevance — names cities served, links to city pages -->
      <div class="sd-local">
        <h3>Ductwork &amp; Airflow Experts in the Murrieta-Temecula Valley</h3>
        <p>We've designed, repaired, and sealed ductwork across Southwest Riverside County for over 20 years — and we've fixed a lot of comfort problems that other companies tried to solve by selling a new unit.</p>
        <p>We serve homes and businesses across <a href="/murrieta/">Murrieta</a>, <a href="/temecula/">Temecula</a>, <a href="/menifee/">Menifee</a>, <a href="/wildomar/">Wildomar</a>, <a href="/lake-elsinore/">Lake Elsinore</a>, Canyon Lake, Sun City, Winchester, French Valley, and Perris.</p>
      </div>

      <a href="tel:9516343233" class="btn btn-red btn-lg">Call About Ductwork</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- OUR PROCESS — numbered timeline -->
<section class="sv-process" aria-labelledby="ductwork-process-heading">
  <div class="sv-process-in">
    <div class="sv-process-hd">
      <div class="eyebrow">How It Works</div>
      <h2 id="ductwork-process-heading">Our Ductwork <em>Process</em></h2>
      <p>Diagnose the real problem first, then fix it right.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sv-steps">
      <div class="sv-step">
        <div class="sv-step-n">1</div>
        <div class="sv-step-bd">
          <h3>Airflow Diagnosis & Duct Inspection</h3>
          <p>We measure airflow at the registers, inspect accessible duct runs in the attic and crawlspace, and find what's actually causing the hot rooms, weak vents, or high bills — leaks, crushed runs, bad design, or undersized ducts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sv-step">
        <div class="sv-step-n">2</div>
        <div class="sv-step-bd">
          <h3>Clear Findings & Written Quote</h3>
          <p>We show you what we found and explain the options in plain terms — repair, seal, rework, or replace. You get a written, itemized estimate and an honest take on what's worth doing and what isn't.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sv-step">
        <div class="sv-step-n">3</div>
        <div class="sv-step-bd">
          <h3>Professional Repair, Sealing or Install</h3>
          <p>Our technicians do the work — sealing leaks, replacing damaged runs, reworking bad design, or installing new ductwork — with proper materials and clean connections that hold up.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sv-step">
        <div class="sv-step-n">4</div>
        <div class="sv-step-bd">
          <h3>Test & Verify the Fix</h3>
          <p>We re-check airflow at the registers and confirm the rooms that were a problem are actually fixed. We don't call it done until the comfort issue is solved, not just the visible damage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SERVICE FAQ -->
<section class="faq-sec" aria-labelledby="ductwork-faq-heading">
  <div class="faq-container">
    <div class="faq-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Common Questions</div>
      <h2 id="ductwork-faq-heading">Ductwork &amp; Airflow FAQs</h2>
      <p>Straight answers about ductwork and airflow in the Murrieta-Temecula Valley. Don't see your question? Call <a href="tel:9516343233">(951) 634-3233</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Why is one room in my house always hotter or colder than the rest?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Uneven room temperatures are almost always a duct or airflow problem, not an equipment problem. The duct run to that room may be leaking, crushed, disconnected, too long, or undersized — so it never gets its share of conditioned air. Replacing the AC or furnace won&#x27;t fix it. We diagnose the airflow, find the actual cause, and fix that.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How do I know if my ducts are leaking?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Common signs: rooms that won&#x27;t reach temperature, vents with weak airflow, energy bills that keep rising while the equipment seems fine, excessive dust, and an attic or crawlspace that feels conditioned. A meaningful share of conditioned air in a typical home leaks out of the ducts before it reaches the rooms. We can inspect and measure to confirm.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is duct sealing worth it?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">For most homes with leaky ducts, yes — you&#x27;re currently paying to heat and cool your attic and crawlspace. Sealing the leaks means the air you condition actually reaches your rooms, which improves comfort and reduces how hard your equipment has to work. We&#x27;ll tell you honestly whether sealing will make a real difference in your specific home.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can you add ductwork for an addition or remodel?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Yes. We design and install new ductwork for additions, remodels, and new construction — sized and laid out properly so the new space is comfortable and the existing system isn&#x27;t overtaxed. Adding square footage without planning the ductwork is a common reason additions never feel right.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>My airflow is weak at every vent — what causes that?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Whole-home weak airflow can come from undersized or restrictive ductwork, inadequate return air, a dirty blower or filter, crushed main trunk lines, or poor original design. It&#x27;s a diagnosis, not a guess — we measure and inspect to find which of those it is, because the fix is different for each.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Will fixing my ducts lower my energy bills?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">Often, yes. When ducts leak or are poorly designed, your equipment runs longer and harder to compensate — and you still aren&#x27;t comfortable. Sealing leaks and correcting airflow means the system does its job in less run time. The size of the savings depends on how bad the duct problems are to start with.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do I need new ductwork or just repairs?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">It depends on the condition and design of what you have. Sometimes targeted sealing and a few run replacements solve the problem; sometimes the original design is the problem and reworking it is the real fix. We inspect first and give you an honest recommendation — we&#x27;re not going to sell you a full duct replacement you don&#x27;t need.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do you offer free estimates on ductwork?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">We provide free estimates on ductwork installation and replacement projects. An airflow diagnosis or duct inspection may carry a diagnostic fee, which we&#x27;ll tell you about upfront. Call (951) 634-3233 for current rates and to schedule.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-cta">
      <p>Still have questions? We're here to help.</p>
      <a href="tel:9516343233" class="btn btn-red">Call Steve</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

